{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "or-reviewer-decisions-2026-11-25",
		"name": "OpenRegister Reviewer Decisions API",
		"description": "A reviewer owns their decision, through the route (change reviewer-owns-their-decisions, task 1.3; REQ-ROD-001).\n\nTwo reviewers in one group, which the schema lets read and update its objects, under x-openregister-review ownership decider. A file on an object names a BSN; extraction makes it an entity with one relation on the file. The first reviewer decides (PATCH /api/entity-relations/{id}, 200, a decision uuid), the second is refused with 403 decision-owned naming that decision and its decider, the relation read back carries the first decision unchanged, and the first reviewer may still change their own (recorded as a new decision superseding the first).\n\nAn object's file sits in the openregister account's home, which no reviewer has a mount on; the relation is then decided by the object's update rule. Before that, every reviewer was refused no_write_access_to_relation_subject, so the ownership rule was never reached through the route.\n\nEach run makes its own valid BSN (eleven test): extraction is keyed on a file's content and entities are shared by value. A save of the file settings replaces them, so they are read first, the save sends the whole set with only the recognition keys changed, and the whole set is restored at the end.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
